For over seven years, my journey as a technical writer has been both transformative and deeply fulfilling. When I first stepped into the corporate world as an intern, fresh out of college, I knew little about technical writing. However, I was certain about my passion for helping people, solving problems, and approaching challenges with a solution-oriented mindset.
As I gradually embraced technical writing as a career, I discovered how impactful clear documentation can be. I realized that my work could genuinely help users overcome real-life challenges, guide them through complex processes, and reduce the risk of customers getting stuck. This sense of purpose made me fall in love with the profession.
Throughout my career, I have gained hands-on experience with leading software authoring tools such as Madcap Flare, Oxygen XML, CCMS, and DITA. I have also worked extensively with product management tools like JIRA, Confluence, wikis, Kanban boards, and agile methodologies. Each project has strengthened my belief in the value of well-crafted documentation.
These seven years have been an amazing journey of growth and learning. Now, I am excited to expand my skill set further by exploring new domains like product management and banking, while continuing to find joy in making technology accessible and understandable for everyone.
